# Managed by gx10-cluster ansible (roles/cluster). Local edits are overwritten.
#
# Peer addresses on the interconnect, one line per peer per subnet:
#
#     <peer-name> <address>
#
# Read by gx10-interconnect so the tool needs no inventory of its own. No
# subnet index column: the tool matches each address to the local interface on
# the same /24, which stays right if the subnets are ever reordered.
#
# The peer NAME is the management name, deliberately: gx10-interconnect --peer
# starts its RDMA server over SSH, and SSH must not depend on the very link
# the probe is trying to test.
#
# Interconnect members only (cluster_index defined): this file is what
# twonode.sh and `ws check` read to pick their rank-1, and a peer with no
# cable has no interconnect address to name - listing one would put a
# mesh-only box at the head of an alphabetized group and make every two-node
# launch on the pair point at it. The task that writes this file is itself
# skipped on such a node; the filter here is what keeps it right for its
# cabled peers.
{% for h in groups['gx10'] if h != inventory_hostname and hostvars[h].cluster_index is defined %}
{% for s in cluster_subnets %}
{{ h }} {{ s }}.{{ hostvars[h].cluster_index }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
